{"sentences": [{"sentence_id": "s1", "sentence": "Thirty-three trials of BTK inhibitors are recorded in multiple sclerosis (MS), with 18 in Phase 3, 11 in Phase 2, and 4 in Phase 1.", "cites": ["NCT06104683"]}, {"sentence_id": "s2", "sentence": "Sponsors include Sanofi (10 trials), Roche and Merck KGaA (5 each), Novartis (4), and smaller contributions from Zenas BioPharma, Guangzhou Lupeng, and others.", "cites": ["NCT06104683"]}, {"sentence_id": "s3", "sentence": "Six trials have stopped, including five evobrutinib trials (Merck KGaA) terminated due to lack of efficacy or changes in trial design.", "cites": ["NCT04338022"]}, {"sentence_id": "s4", "sentence": "Current development includes Phase 3 trials of fenebrutinib (Roche), remibrutinib (Novartis), and tolebrutinib (Sanofi), and Phase 2 studies of rocbrutinib (Lupeng) and orelabrutinib (Zenas).", "cites": ["NCT04586010"]}, {"sentence_id": "s5", "sentence": "Evobrutinib failed to meet its primary endpoint of annualized relapse rate in two Phase 3 trials (NCT04338022, NCT04338061) and one Phase 2 trial (NCT02975349), all terminated.", "cites": ["NCT02975349"]}, {"sentence_id": "s6", "sentence": "Evobrutinib’s maximum phase in MS is 3, with no approvals, and its development in relapsing MS was stopped due to lack of efficacy versus teriflunomide.", "cites": ["CHEMBL4072833"]}, {"sentence_id": "s7", "sentence": "Pirtobrutinib (Loxo Oncology) was withdrawn from a Phase 2 MS trial (NCT06104683) for sponsor decision, with no plans to continue.", "cites": ["NCT06104683"]}, {"sentence_id": "s8", "sentence": "A 2026 review notes that BTK inhibitors target both adaptive and innate immunity, with modulation of myeloid cell and microglial activation relevant to MS pathology.", "cites": ["PMID:42518914"]}, {"sentence_id": "s9", "sentence": "Recent literature (2026) indicates BTK inhibitors show promising effects on inflammatory activity in MS, with emerging signals on disability progression.", "cites": ["PMID:42518914"]}, {"s